<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugh of Bruyeres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Hugh de la Bruyère</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugh of Bruyeres was a crusader knight from Champagne who received the Barony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karytaina">Karytaina</a>, one of the largest fiefs of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, around 1209. He held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skorta">Skorta</a> highlands of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpheios">Alpheios</a> valley. His son Geoffrey of Bruyeres became celebrated as the model of chivalry in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-the-morea">Chronicle of the Morea</a>.</p></div>
